  158: - Job prequalification / contract status data (contract amount, billed amount, percent complete, PM) → "/service/prequals" ("PreQuals")
  159: - AP vendor statement reconciliation (manual line-by-line comparison of a vendor statement against Vista) → "/service/ap/statement-reconciliations" ("Statement Reconciliations"); a tab with `?tab=` (this route has no other query param, so it's the first one, not `&tab=`) — valid values `statements` (the default: reconcile by vendor reference/amount) and `jobs` (reconcile a job-cost statement by job number/amount instead)
> 160: - Vendor quote / proforma PDF import (extract a quote's line items, reconcile against HQMT pricing/parts, and add the PO to a batch) now happens ON the Purchase Order Entry screen, not a screen of its own: "/purchase-orders/entry/edit?co=<co>&mth=<YYYY-MM-01>&batchId=<id>" ("Purchase Order Entry"). Adding a PO with "Add PO" replaces that button with "Import from Quote" until the draft is saved, so only one PO is entered at a time. The quote's header fields and line rows land in the batch grid for review, warnings about what the document didn't say appear above it, and anything required but unreadable is highlighted red. The quote PDFs themselves are local files the user picks, so they are NOT addressable — never generate a link to a specific quote, only to a batch. There is no longer a "/purchase-orders/proforma-import" route; rewrite any such link to the batch editor above. Requires the "Create / edit purchase orders" permission.
  161: - Vendor insurance & signed-agreement compliance (COI expiration dates, MSA/PSA/TSA agreements on file) → "/service/ap/vendor-compliance" ("Vendor Compliance")
  162: - Vendor master record (a vendor's address, phone, payment method / EFT setup, tax & 1099 fields, hold codes, additional remit addresses, notes) → "/service/ap/vendor-details" ("Vendor Details"); deep-link one vendor with `/service/ap/vendor-details?vendor=<vendorCode>`, and a tab with `&tab=` — valid values `grid` (the vendor list), `info`, `addlInfo`, `paymentMethod`, `icReportInfo`, `notes`, `addlAddresses`, `vendorCompliance`, `vendorHoldCodes`. The page publishes the open tab and the selected vendor in Session context — read the vendor from there rather than asking. Requires the "View vendor details" permission, and the `vendorCompliance` tab additionally requires the Vendor Compliance permission; a user without either sees no such tab, so don't promise it.

